# 7. Reverse Integer

## Problem

Given a signed 32-bit integer `x`, return `x` with its digits reversed. If reversing `x` causes the value to go outside the signed 32-bit integer range, return `0`.

## Algorithm

1. Check whether the number is positive or negative.
2. Store its sign.
3. Reverse the digits using string slicing.
4. Restore the original sign.
5. Check if the reversed number is within the 32-bit signed integer range.
6. Return the reversed number if valid; otherwise return `0`.

## Time Complexity

O(n)

## Space Complexity

O(n)
